into more casual recreational use.&nbsp;

01:44:50.360 --> 01:44:51.400
Kevin Rose: Right.
Tim Ferriss: In which case, it's very&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:51.400 --> 01:44:56.760
important for me to say that ketamine can be very&nbsp;
helpful for people with, say, treatment-resistant&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:44:56.760 --> 01:45:02.640
depression or chronic depression. If you use it&nbsp;
chronically though, it flips the other way and it&nbsp;&nbsp;

01:45:02.640 --> 01:45:08.268
actually makes you predisposed to more depression.&nbsp;
So it's just something for people to be aware of.&nbsp;

01:45:08.268 --> 01:45:12.204
Kevin Rose: Yeah.
Tim Ferriss: And as is true with so many things —&nbsp;

01:45:12.204 --> 01:45:13.287
Kevin Rose: Oh, my God.
Tim Ferriss: More is not better.&nbsp;

01:45:13.287 --> 01:45:16.080
Kevin Rose: Do you know what — what was the&nbsp;
drug that Michael Jackson died of? Do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

